<pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I09fb2be3132c2cb0f9316d620e2bb07a2f7d7ae4" commit="2b0358eda6560aab03075aa257d79757118aaefe" commit_message="FROMLIST: usb: dwc2: host: Fix ahbcfg for rk3066  The comment for ahbcfg for rk3066 parameters (also used for rk3288) claimed that ahbcfg was INCR16, but it wasn't.  Since the bits weren't shifted properly, the 0x7 ended up being masked and we ended up programming 0x3 for the HBstLen.  Let's set it to INCR16 properly.  As per Wu Liang Feng at Rockchip this may increase transmission efficiency.  I did blackbox tests with writing 0s to a USB-based SD reader (forcefully capping CPU Freq to try to measure efficiency):   cd /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu0/cpufreq   echo userspace &gt; scaling_governor   echo 126000 &gt; scaling_setspeed   for i in $(seq 10); do     dd if=/dev/zero of=/dev/sdb bs=1M count=750   done  With the above tests I found that speeds went from ~15MB/s to ~18MB/s. Note that most other tests I did (including reading from the same USB reader) didn't show any difference in performance.  BUG=None TEST=better perf; Using mem: (r(0xff540008) &gt;&gt; 1) &amp; 0xf =&gt; 7L  Change-Id: I09fb2be3132c2cb0f9316d620e2bb07a2f7d7ae4 Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/7453801/) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/307162 " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="307162" owner_email="dianders@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/62/307162/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I92248ad5e77270629b695f2e60f0e458ab33c545" commit="36d0aad4c7502b9a4b6920e3fb546ccaaafded55" commit_message="Wizpig: change baseboard to Strago  Wizpig is a Braswell project, so using Strago as its baseboard. In addition, added the scripts for factory wiping and battery cut-off.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:42916 TEST=setup board and build packages  Change-Id: I92248ad5e77270629b695f2e60f0e458ab33c545 Signed-off-by: Kaiyen Chang &lt;kaiyen.chang@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/304115 Reviewed-by: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="304115" owner_email="kaiyen.chang@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" ref="refs/changes/15/304115/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I261efd8c2ce5f998ff70881cf091c6af950c3586" commit="bcedb40e18b85adf54d4a59d19733fe5e5e9a29d" commit_message="Exposes the chrome instance used by chromedriver instance.  There are cases where clients of chromedriver.ChromeDriver objects need to use Chrome to create tabs and do some kind of verification.  We can use the same chrome object that the driver already, while the driver is active and hasn't been closed.  That way we can avoid creating a new logging session.  Example: crosreview.com/304081 will need this feature.  BUG=None. TEST=None.  Change-Id: I261efd8c2ce5f998ff70881cf091c6af950c3586 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/307561 Commit-Ready: Mussa Kiroga &lt;mussa@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mussa Kiroga &lt;mussa@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mussa Kiroga &lt;mussa@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="307561" owner_email="mussa@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/61/307561/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Id0808450ee4dbc06e830c6c67a0883382169dacb" commit="5768fb9f2411a2efd67cda4f84d13903fad35268" commit_message="UPSTREAM: usb: gadget: udc: core: Fix argument of dma_map_single for IOMMU  The dma_map_single and dma_unmap_single should set &quot;gadget-&gt;dev.parent&quot; instead of &quot;&amp;gadget-&gt;dev&quot; in the first argument because the parent has a udc controller's device pointer. Otherwise, iommu functions are not called in ARM environment.  BUG=none TEST=build and boot Smaug, XUSB device mode still works  Signed-off-by: Yoshihiro Shimoda &lt;yoshihiro.shimoda.uh@renesas.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Felipe Balbi &lt;balbi@ti.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit 7ace8fc8219e4cbbfd5b4790390d9a01a2541cdf) Signed-off-by: Mark Kuo &lt;mkuo@nvidia.com&gt;  Change-Id: Id0808450ee4dbc06e830c6c67a0883382169dacb Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/307029 Commit-Ready: Mark Kuo &lt;mkuo@nvidia.com&gt; Tested-by: Mark Kuo &lt;mkuo@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="307029" owner_email="mkuo@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/29/307029/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I230fdc3f1ec62a8cfa91a36621513b169791b20d" commit="12e9a5d2d388511972495ad26f6b37ddced4a711" commit_message="chameleon: Read chameleon_host/port attribute on moblab  Allow chameleon_host/port to be specified just like servo_host/port on moblab.  BUG=chromium:545385 TEST=Run display_Resolution.extended test on Moblab.  Change-Id: I230fdc3f1ec62a8cfa91a36621513b169791b20d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/307007 Commit-Ready: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wai-Hong Tam &lt;waihong@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="307007" owner_email="drinkcat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googles